From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:04:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] scrobj: component events (<event>, fireEvent) reach connected
 sinks

The <event> elements of a component's <public> are kept. A component that has events supports
IConnectionPointContainer (one connection point, for the dispinterface of its events), and
IProvideClassInfo2 whose class information is made as a type library has it: the component's
interface, an events dispinterface with one method for each event, and a coclass in which the events
are the default source. fireEvent(name) in the component's script calls that event, by name,
on each connected sink; an event it does not declare is ignored. The type library
Scriptlet.TypeLib writes gets the events as a source interface too.

diff --git a/dlls/scrobj/scrobj.c b/dlls/scrobj/scrobj.c
